body:
tl/dr - RESOLVED WITH WORKAROUND. This is a bug in how prerender works. 

Well, I went ahead and investigated and found the problem. The server side rendered view for index.html (the one used for template engine) already has the <meta> tags from the app-root while it should only have those meta tags which are explicitly in the index.html. This happens for any element created in the head region. The workaround was to change the prerender code to remove these extra meta tags as follows. This also repros with Renderer. So its not just a Meta Service issue but a deeper issue.

Look at the html.replace part. That's the workaround.

renderModuleFactory(AppServerModuleNgFactory, {
  document: index,
  url: '/',
  extraProviders: [
    provideModuleMap(LAZY_MODULE_MAP)
  ]
})
.then(html => writeFileSync(join('browser', 'index.html'), html.replace(new RegExp('<meta name="[a-z]+:[a-z_]+" content="[A-Za-z0-9 ,\'!:/\. -]+">', 'g'), '').replace(new RegExp('<meta property="[a-z]+:[a-z_]+" content="[A-Za-z0-9,\'!:/\. -]+">', 'g'), '').replace(new RegExp('<meta name="[a-z]+" content="[A-Za-z0-9,\'!:/\. -]+">', 'g'), '')));
